statement:
A \term{category} consists of:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1.4em]
\item objects;
\item arrows, each with a specified source and target, written $f:A\to B$;
\item an identity arrow $1_A:A\to A$ for each object;
\item a composite $g\circ f:A\to C$ whenever $f:A\to B$ and $g:B\to C$.
\end{itemize}
Composition obeys two laws:
\begin{align*}
 (h\circ g)\circ f&=h\circ(g\circ f)
 &&\text{(associativity)},\\
 1_B\circ f&=f=f\circ1_A
 &&\text{(identity laws)}.
\end{align*}
Here $f:A\to B$, $g:B\to C$ and $h:C\to D$ have matching endpoints.

A candidate state $x=(\ell,f,\gamma,\kappa)$ on $\mathcal K_n$ is legal when
\begin{enumerate}[label=(A\arabic*),leftmargin=2.4em]
\item both roots lie in $R_n$, and $\ell(A)\ne\ell(B)$;
\item a dancer at a place of index $i$ faces the place of index $i+n$, that
  is, across the centre;
\item each gesture lies in the declared gesture alphabet, and the pair
  $(\gamma(A),\gamma(B))$ lies in the declared mirror relation, which says
  which gesture a partner must show in reply: an offered right hand asks for
  a receiving left;
\item if $\kappa$ is present then both roots are orbit sites $v_i$ and $v_j$
  with $j-i=n$ modulo $2n$, and $\kappa$ names one hand of each dancer and
  the centre $o$.
\end{enumerate}

An equation may be:
\begin{description}[style=nextline,leftmargin=1.4em,labelindent=0pt]
\item[Definition] introduces a symbol, as in $z(p):=$ the number of
  zeros of $p$;
\item[Identity] follows from prior structure, as in
  $\sum_{i}\bigl(p(v_i)-p(v_{i-1})\bigr)=0$ around the square;
\item[Invariant constraint] selects legal states, as the walker's
  $p(v_0)+p(v_1)+p(v_2)+p(v_3)=1$, a sum of integers, does among the tables
  of zeros and ones;
\item[Evolution rule] maps one state to another, as in
  $p'(v_i)=p(v_{i-1})$;
\item[Recognizer] tests a pattern or observable, as in $p_2=p_0$, with $p_t$
  the state after $t$ ticks: true exactly when opposite corners agree.
\end{description}

A connection with link table $U$ is
\begin{description}[style=nextline,leftmargin=1.4em,labelindent=0pt,itemsep=.15em]
\item[face-flat] when $F^{v_f}_U(f)=1$ for every face $f$, with $v_f$ any
corner of $f$ (by \cref{def:curvature-general} the choice does not matter);
\item[loop-flat] when $\Hol_U(\gamma)=1$ for every based loop $\gamma$ in the
transport skeleton;
\item[pure gauge] when there are elements $c_v\in G$ with
\begin{equation}
U_e=c_{t(e)}\,c_{s(e)}^{-1}
\quad\text{for every oriented edge.}

\end{equation}
\end{description}
The elements $c_v$ are \role{WITNESS} data about a connection state, not
further link coordinates.

Under the hypotheses of \cref{thm:curie}:
\begin{enumerate}
\item a run keeps the symmetry $S$ at every tick if and only if it stays
  among the states that $S$ fixes;
\item a deterministic realizer that commutes with $G$ exists if and only if
  at every legal state some allowed batch is fixed by every motion that
  fixes the state;
\item averaging any realizer over the motions of $G$ gives a stochastic
  realizer that commutes with $G$.
\end{enumerate}
